WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-RO

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.440
Hello!  Welcome back to Lam Rim.

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:12.580
Today we will review the entire course.  It

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:16.520
's good for me.  I would like to do a review for myself.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:20.680
This format where you participate in separate episodes

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:24.520
and at different times

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:26.880
can make you lose the structure of the entire teaching.  I

00:00:27.599 --> 00:00:30.559
thought it would be nice if today we started

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:34.560
from the beginning and went through the structure of the

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.280
entire Lam Rim teaching that we have been through.  I'm going to

00:00:38.559 --> 00:00:42.799
go through all the ideas based on IDIMs, the IDea IMaginilor,

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:47.540
which we use to teach ACI teachers.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:49.220
ACI teachers

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:52.800
should be able to look at one of these images

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:56.480
and identify the idea behind it.

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:59.120
Tim, how many images did I say there would be?   A thousand or so?  How

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:02.800
many?

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:08.639
500 or something like that.  It's easy to give an exam,

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:12.493
to examine someone based on images alone.  We're just showing you these pictures

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:14.160
.

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:17.800
So I challenge you that during this review

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:20.240
when I show you an image I'm going to

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:24.000
give you a second to see if you

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:26.533
remember what that image was about.

00:01:26.533 --> 00:01:28.000
And so we will do a good review

00:01:28.799 --> 00:01:32.479
of the entire course we took.  Okay.  Let's begin...

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:36.560
First photo, Mr.  The seats.

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:42.000
This image should remind you

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:47.420
that we are in the middle of practices

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:50.360
for people with average motivation.

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:52.440
And that they are trying to achieve nirvana.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:58.800
They are trying to get out of the wheel of life, out of all their personal suffering.

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:02.560
Here the Buddha taught the three trainings

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:07.120
that will help you reach personal nirvana.

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:12.420
The third training is understanding emptiness, understanding PIX.

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:15.880
The second training is meditation.

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:21.200
On a deep level, these two practices can only be done in a quiet place,

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:26.880
at certain times of the day, when you are truly focused while sitting on the meditation cushion.

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:31.740
On a deep level, these two need to be done

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:34.865
at special times of the day.

00:02:34.865 --> 00:02:39.540
But this, the foundation for the two, which is to be good to other people,

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:41.280
[which] you can call morality, you

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:43.840
can call it an ethical way of life,

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:48.800
but ultimately it is [the idea] of being good to other people.

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:50.840
This is the foundation

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.640
that is always at our fingertips throughout the day.

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:57.900
This is one of the three great trainings of Buddhism,

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:00.659
designed to help us achieve nirvana.

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:04.049
And it's at our fingertips all day long.

00:03:04.049 --> 00:03:05.360
In this image you

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:10.360
can see Seiji helping Geshe Michael with the computer,

00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:14.640
which is one of the nicest things young people can do for the elderly.

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:20.959
Next picture... See if you remember what this picture was about?  Did

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:27.040
you guess?

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:34.080
This lady is calculating her taxes.  What does it mean that she is doing in this Lam Rim system?  It

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:35.320
makes her...

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:41.360
...a Dharma Master.   When I say Dharma Master, or Tantric Master,

00:03:42.159 --> 00:03:44.544
I know what image you have in your mind:

00:03:44.544 --> 00:03:48.140
a great lama on a throne wearing a big yellow hat.

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:57.760
Maybe he's ringing a bell and beating a small drum and it's...

00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:00.751
And you think, "This is a Dharma Master. This is a real Dharma Master."

00:04:00.751 --> 00:04:02.900
Or you think of the old picture of Nagarjuna.

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:06.739
And he is mystical in every way.

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:10.959
In Lam Rim I learned

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:13.920
that a simple woman

00:04:14.799 --> 00:04:17.439
who has two children, is married,

00:04:18.239 --> 00:04:22.078
is a Dharma Master.  She is a true Dharma Master.

00:04:22.639 --> 00:04:27.459
Pabongka Rinpoche said, “Do not think that a Dharma Master must sit on a throne

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:30.660
reciting a tantric ritual.”

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:33.960
What is this lady doing?

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:37.760
He pays his taxes on time.

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:42.840
Calculating taxes correctly is really difficult in my country [USA].  It

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:46.320
could take weeks to calculate your taxes,

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:48.880
to calculate them carefully,

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:51.040
to calculate them properly,

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:53.759
to pay every penny you should pay.

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:56.400
This makes her...

00:04:56.479 --> 00:05:00.639
She has the first of the extraordinary trainings of a good person,

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:02.880
she has kindness towards other people.  This is what

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:05.400
a true Dharma Master does.

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:09.920
Forget [about] those images you have of lots of lamas with big hats on their heads,

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:11.700
and bells ringing.  That's easy.

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:13.420
Anyone can do this.

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:16.720
Being nice to people is difficult [especially in difficult, crisis situations].

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:20.079
Maintaining your morality, maintaining your ethics

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:22.065
is also difficult.

00:05:22.065 --> 00:05:24.700
Next.  I'll give you

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:30.080
a moment.  Do you remember what it's about?  The

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:39.240
quote from Lam Rim was @TSUL KHRIMS LDAN PA'I DGE SLONG 'OD DANG LDAN.

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:42.560
A person who truly keeps their vows,

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:46.720
who truly keeps the Buddhist guidelines, especially the 10 precepts,

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:49.620
shines, really shines.

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:58.656
A person who makes a healthy, modest, constant effort to keep their commitments,

00:05:58.656 --> 00:06:01.360
to stick to the ten good deeds,

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:04.000
and to be good to other people.

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:07.519
[She] has a kind of peaceful look on her face, she's

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:10.160
glowing.

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:12.260
When he walks into a room, you know it.

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:17.360
Everyone starts to feel better, like Tim and Seiji.

00:06:18.340 --> 00:06:19.860
This is a light of the world.

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:23.240
Buddha said, "Those people are the light of the world."

00:06:24.640 --> 00:06:26.380
There is a Christian expression:

00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:32.400
"Don't put a candle under a bushel, let the world see your happy face."

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:39.960
And this is a true guiding light for the entire world.

00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:43.440
Next image IDIM#4

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:57.600
This is a rock that I climbed with my partner Veronica, for her birthday, during this Lam Rim.

00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:06.940
We were talking about sunset, for which the Tibetan word is @NUB PA.

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:10.580
It is also the word for west, because the sun sets in the west.

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:12.500
@NUB PA means

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:16.080
sunset and that is a very sad verb.

00:07:16.880 --> 00:07:20.820
This is a very sad idea in dharma.

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:27.980
The most famous place is at the end of the book Abhidharmakosha - the Treasury of Higher Wisdom.

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:31.760
"The Treasury of Higher Wisdom" is written by Master Vasabhandu.  And he says:

00:07:32.960 --> 00:07:39.060
"The sun of Dharma, the light of Dharma, will set in this world."

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:43.440
"We will lose the light of Dharma in this world."  "This world will go into darkness."

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:45.520
"After a certain period of time, the

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:49.560
Buddha's teachings will disappear in this world."

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:56.060
"They will first disappear from people's minds, but they will still be in libraries."

00:07:56.060 --> 00:07:59.600
Those books are still in libraries.  Probably libraries that John Brady hasn't found yet.

00:08:00.319 --> 00:08:04.239
"And then later, they will disappear from libraries and then they will be taken away."  I

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:11.840
put the image here because Pabongka Rinpoche pointed out a special idea.  He said,

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:19.520
"If you cannot keep your commitments, if you cannot behave nicely towards other people,

00:08:19.740 --> 00:08:22.640
then we can say that the Dharma has left this world."

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:26.319
The light of Dharma has left this world within you.

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:30.780
The sun has set in your own chest,

00:08:30.780 --> 00:08:34.460
which would be a very sad thing if we did not keep our vows.  The

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:36.560
next picture.

00:08:43.280 --> 00:08:48.200
We called this retreat "Love in the Time of Virus."

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:55.440
The point is that if during a very difficult time in the world, you

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:57.600
keep your commitments,

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:00.860
you're good to other people,

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:04.320
when things are scary and scary and the virus is spreading, we

00:09:04.320 --> 00:09:06.160
don't know where, we don't know how, and we do

00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:08.880
n't know how many people are going to die.

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:16.660
If in those difficult times you do something good towards other people,

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:19.160
it is much, much more powerful.

00:09:19.360 --> 00:09:22.420
If you remember, he mentioned a 5-star Buddha paradise,

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:25.759
which is like a perfect place.

00:09:26.399 --> 00:09:29.839
It's easy to be a good person, everyone there is a good person.  That's

00:09:30.560 --> 00:09:33.236
not a big achievement.                                            It's no big deal.

00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:35.220
And the seed is not that strong --

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:38.580
to be nice in a group of nice people.

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:42.880
To be good when people attack you, when people are afraid,

00:09:43.839 --> 00:09:47.518
when people are not good to each other, and to be the only person

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:54.060
who comes forward and gives things away during a difficult time -

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:57.340
then that is an extremely pure person.

00:09:57.520 --> 00:10:01.500
This is powerful karma.  It's incredible karma, much stronger.

00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:03.840
I think the coming of this virus is a very good moment, and

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:09.120
it's a very good chance for all of us to show:

00:10:09.280 --> 00:10:14.380
- Are we really true Buddhists?   Are we really practicing the bodhisattva path?

00:10:14.400 --> 00:10:18.560
Can we help others even when things are very difficult?  The

00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:21.500
next picture.  This one

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:31.460
is hard to remember, I'm having trouble remembering what it's about.  I'm going to

00:10:31.700 --> 00:10:36.280
give you some extra time to think about what this image represents.

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:43.840
Pabongka Rinpoche quotes a few books

00:10:44.959 --> 00:10:46.959
with a very, very common ending for different books.  The

00:10:47.360 --> 00:10:57.760
famous quote he quoted is @BLO BZANG RGYAL BA'I BSTAN PA... CIG

00:10:58.780 --> 00:11:02.720
May the teachings of the victorious

00:11:03.519 --> 00:11:05.519
Lobsang Drakpa, Je Tsongkapa

00:11:06.079 --> 00:11:08.079
spread throughout this world.  You're

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:12.720
thinking we need to go online

00:11:12.720 --> 00:11:16.000
and translate this Lam Rim into multiple languages.  We

00:11:17.279 --> 00:11:21.679
must try to spread the good word to as many people as possible.

00:11:22.560 --> 00:11:31.200
This is the end of the prayer and we should exit this Lam Rim session or this video.

00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:35.860
And we should share the Dharma with other people.  We

00:11:35.860 --> 00:11:38.280
should spread Dharma in the world.

00:11:38.400 --> 00:11:44.260
In this part of Lam Rim, Pabongka Rinpoche said,

00:11:44.320 --> 00:11:50.660
“The place where you should spread the Dharma is here, in your heart.”

00:11:50.900 --> 00:11:56.160
Don't think that spreading the Dharma means translating videos

00:11:56.160 --> 00:12:00.800
into multiple languages ​​or anything like that.  This is a very important spread of the Dharma.

00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:05.240
But, he says, "If you spread Dharma within your heart,

00:12:05.920 --> 00:12:09.920
then of course it will spread outside of you because the world comes from your heart."

00:12:09.920 --> 00:12:11.519
From the heart chakra, actually.

00:12:12.320 --> 00:12:16.860
Next image #7

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:23.300
Try to remember what this image was about.  I'll leave you for a second.

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:31.680
This is a favorite topic of mine:

00:12:32.240 --> 00:12:42.000
having a personal relationship with another person, like these two people have.

00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:47.866
In my opinion and in tantra, it is one of the happiest things that can happen to you.

00:12:47.866 --> 00:12:51.860
It's one of the greatest things that can happen to you.

00:12:52.800 --> 00:12:57.520
Anyone can tell you the reason why the whole world is looking for a partner.

00:12:58.399 --> 00:13:00.082
The reason is that it makes people happy.

00:13:00.082 --> 00:13:03.279
It is one of the greatest joys when things go well.

00:13:04.399 --> 00:13:07.518
It's one of the greatest joys you can have, but

00:13:08.399 --> 00:13:12.799
we both know that when it doesn't go well,

00:13:13.519 --> 00:13:16.159
it's one of the greatest misfortunes in life.

00:13:16.959 --> 00:13:19.839
Why is this relevant to this course here?

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:29.120
If your morality is good,

00:13:29.280 --> 00:13:31.360
it is the happiest thing in your life.

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:37.040
And if you violate your morality, the same thing will make you unhappy.

00:13:37.240 --> 00:13:40.320
It's like having a man or woman you like who is your partner,

00:13:41.280 --> 00:13:44.620
and the same person who makes you completely happy

00:13:44.660 --> 00:13:47.860
can also make you completely unhappy.

00:13:48.280 --> 00:13:52.400
So in this case, the vinaya, your personal practice of being good to others,

00:13:52.940 --> 00:13:56.240
your good behavior, is compared to a partner

00:13:56.240 --> 00:13:59.540
who can be the best thing in your life

00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:03.320
or the worst thing in your life - the same person.

00:14:04.060 --> 00:14:10.120
Next IDIM #8

00:14:11.440 --> 00:14:13.840
That was a complicated one.  Can you remember?  I'm going to

00:14:15.519 --> 00:14:17.519
take a sip of my green drink.

00:14:18.639 --> 00:14:20.639
Thank you, Vimala.

00:14:29.440 --> 00:14:33.560
This actually represents breaking your commitments.

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:39.720
Pulling out a weed represents breaking your commitments.

00:14:39.760 --> 00:14:45.260
Why is destroying this plant a breach of commitment?

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:51.560
If you're a gardener, you know you should pull a weed out of the ground

00:14:52.460 --> 00:14:54.640
before the seeds ripen.

00:14:55.420 --> 00:14:59.380
If you wait until the seeds are ready to fall,

00:14:59.920 --> 00:15:01.920
and then pull the plant out of the ground,

00:15:02.160 --> 00:15:04.560
you will scatter about a thousand seeds.

00:15:05.680 --> 00:15:11.260
Next month or next year you'll get thousands of weeds growing.

00:15:11.260 --> 00:15:13.440
So, you will need to attack these weeds early.

00:15:14.480 --> 00:15:19.140
This refers to a very radical statement

00:15:19.360 --> 00:15:21.360
that the Buddha made:

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:27.900
@DGE SLONG DAG SROG DANG BRAL ZHING SHI BA NI BLA'I

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:30.240
It says that it is better to die

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:32.479
than to break your vows.  Why?

00:15:33.680 --> 00:15:35.680
When you break your vows

00:15:35.760 --> 00:15:38.980
you set in motion seeds

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:42.660
that will continue to fall for many lifetimes.

00:15:43.280 --> 00:15:49.740
If you die, you destroy a single mind-body entity.

00:15:50.480 --> 00:15:54.060
If you die, you destroy only one very useful temple,

00:15:54.060 --> 00:15:57.360
a physical temple and a mind.  You lost one life.

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:00.560
But if you break your vows,

00:16:01.279 --> 00:16:04.440
you lose more mind-body ensembles.  You are

00:16:04.440 --> 00:16:07.458
destroying your body and mind for many lifetimes.

00:16:08.240 --> 00:16:11.440
And you have set in motion seeds

00:16:11.440 --> 00:16:14.280
that will destroy many lives.

00:16:14.340 --> 00:16:20.420
Buddha said, "It is better to die than to break your vows," and he

00:16:20.600 --> 00:16:27.460
wasn't being metaphorical.  He was speaking literally

00:16:27.460 --> 00:16:31.280
when he said that.  Better to die than to break your commitments.

00:16:33.360 --> 00:16:35.360
There is a joke in Lam Rim.

00:16:36.880 --> 00:16:44.320
We make a vow to never give up bodhichitta even at the cost of our lives.

00:16:46.720 --> 00:16:52.480
There is a famous statement, our whole lives we wait

00:16:52.720 --> 00:16:54.720
to be thrown in jail

00:16:54.880 --> 00:16:56.880
by certain bad people.

00:16:57.199 --> 00:17:02.479
They come with a knife and say, "Give up your bodhisattva vows or die today."

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:04.799
We will tell [them]:

00:17:04.799 --> 00:17:06.480
"I choose to die."  And they kill us

00:17:06.480 --> 00:17:09.199
.

00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:13.280
I think we've all been waiting for this since we took that oath.

00:17:14.160 --> 00:17:18.300
We're waiting for these guys with knives to show up and threaten us.

00:17:18.300 --> 00:17:22.960
But actually we're the guys with the knives.  We threaten our bodhisattva vows every day.  We

00:17:24.700 --> 00:17:31.840
must make this decision every day when we decide whether or not to keep our vows carefully.

00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:37.860
It's hard to find the guys who will throw you in jail and say,

00:17:38.060 --> 00:17:41.440
"I'll kill you if you don't give up your bodhisattva vows."  The

00:17:44.720 --> 00:17:46.720
next picture.

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:54.540
See if you remember.  I'll give you a minute to try to remember.

00:18:03.840 --> 00:18:05.840
This was a reference....

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:09.039
we have the Mixed Nuts translation team

00:18:09.840 --> 00:18:12.559
and we were translating an old vinaya text.

00:18:13.840 --> 00:18:16.440
The vows of monks, the vows of nuns.

00:18:17.120 --> 00:18:25.140
They were talking about the vow, the custom that you shouldn't...

00:18:25.340 --> 00:18:29.820
...When you become a monk or nun you're given robes, they

00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:31.840
give you a little Buddhist statue,

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:34.960
and they give you a strainer.

00:18:35.919 --> 00:18:39.279
In ancient India you had to carry this strainer with you.

00:18:40.080 --> 00:18:43.360
When drinking water from a stream you

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:49.439
should strain the water first to make sure you don't kill any small insects.

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:55.680
I mentioned a famous custom in the vinaya,

00:18:56.240 --> 00:18:59.200
if two monks go down to the water,

00:18:59.420 --> 00:19:02.380
down to the stream to get water,

00:19:02.640 --> 00:19:07.340
then they should choose the most benevolent monk to check the water.

00:19:09.280 --> 00:19:15.040
Don't choose the one who doesn't care about insects.  Find a guy who loves bugs

00:19:15.840 --> 00:19:19.280
and have him check the water because he'll be more careful.

00:19:20.000 --> 00:19:22.000
What's the idea?

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:26.440
We talked about a type of ecological vow,

00:19:27.040 --> 00:19:31.540
where monks and nuns are not supposed to even pull the leaves of

00:19:31.760 --> 00:19:37.560
a plant, because they are shelter for small creatures.

00:19:38.060 --> 00:19:43.000
This means - to respect even very small vows,

00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:49.180
take them very seriously, because the results multiply exponentially.

00:19:49.180 --> 00:19:53.600
Then, it's important to keep your morality at a very subtle level,

00:19:55.039 --> 00:19:58.399
at a very fine level, and don't analyze them.

00:20:00.559 --> 00:20:02.549
If I were to write the bodhisattva vows, I

00:20:02.549 --> 00:20:04.719
would write an additional bodhisattva vow about

00:20:05.039 --> 00:20:07.199
not analyzing your bodhisattva vows.  There

00:20:07.840 --> 00:20:09.840
's nothing more irritating than

00:20:10.400 --> 00:20:14.420
a person informing you that they're honoring their vows and that's why they

00:20:14.420 --> 00:20:17.760
have to be insensitive today.

00:20:19.760 --> 00:20:23.199
Keep your vows in a pleasant way.  Keep them being happy.  Don't exaggerate.

00:20:23.840 --> 00:20:29.760
Don't bother other people with your vows because vows are not meant to bother other people.

00:20:30.559 --> 00:20:35.279
Keep vows small, keep them quiet.  Keep them to yourself, don't advertise them.

00:20:36.320 --> 00:20:42.159
There is a saying in Islam... Let the left hand not know what the right hand is doing.

00:20:43.039 --> 00:20:46.799
That means not advertising your vows.  Keep them quiet.

00:20:47.440 --> 00:20:49.840
Keep them at a very fine level.  The

00:20:50.559 --> 00:20:52.559
next picture.

00:20:59.200 --> 00:21:04.780
Here is the idea that being kind to others

00:21:05.120 --> 00:21:08.900
is like planting a tree.

00:21:09.180 --> 00:21:12.020
Today I went to the Peach Tree Cafe

00:21:12.120 --> 00:21:14.740
to check something out.

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:19.039
Stanley, Allison, and I planted a peach tree there

00:21:20.640 --> 00:21:23.599
when we first started the morning show, "The Peach Tree."

00:21:24.400 --> 00:21:28.319
And I want to tell you that three peaches came out this week.

00:21:29.120 --> 00:21:31.359
And now we have peaches.

00:21:33.600 --> 00:21:38.820
That means taking care of basic practices.

00:21:38.820 --> 00:21:43.160
Take care of your roots and plant beautiful karma

00:21:43.840 --> 00:21:46.440
by keeping your vows and being kind to others.

00:21:46.440 --> 00:21:48.480
And this will turn into a tree.

00:21:49.039 --> 00:21:51.039
And that peach tree that I planted

00:21:51.840 --> 00:21:53.760
about five months ago is

00:21:53.760 --> 00:21:56.559
already bearing a lot of fruit.

00:21:57.200 --> 00:22:03.540
If you hadn't taken care of it when it was small [the tree], you would have nothing [now].

00:22:03.540 --> 00:22:06.860
If you take care of the foundation of your Buddhist practice,

00:22:07.340 --> 00:22:09.360
which is being kind to other people,

00:22:10.000 --> 00:22:12.800
then the fruits will be thousands and thousands and thousands.

00:22:12.860 --> 00:22:14.820
[The result] will come, it will grow

00:22:14.820 --> 00:22:16.640
...it will turn into a tree

00:22:17.200 --> 00:22:22.080
that will bear peaches every year and you will have fruit for many years.

00:22:22.640 --> 00:22:24.140
Preserve... protect...

00:22:24.320 --> 00:22:28.160
This child carefully protects the shoot.

00:22:28.480 --> 00:22:30.480
Protect your morality.  [Keep your morals]

00:22:31.120 --> 00:22:33.120
Next picture.

00:22:34.880 --> 00:22:39.960
If I remember correctly, there were four conditions

00:22:40.880 --> 00:22:43.760
that could cause you to break your commitments.

00:22:43.760 --> 00:22:45.760
If you've taken your bodhisattva vows

00:22:46.400 --> 00:22:49.039
or you've taken your pratimoksha vinaya vows,

00:22:49.679 --> 00:22:52.399
or even if you've taken your tantric Diamond Way vows

00:22:53.340 --> 00:22:58.799
... I think there were four... ...that Pabongka Rinpoche reviewed... maybe more....

00:22:59.440 --> 00:23:01.440
However, there are certain conditions

00:23:01.680 --> 00:23:03.740
that can "help" you break your vows.

00:23:03.820 --> 00:23:07.880
If you want to break your vows, there are a few ways to do it.  The

00:23:07.880 --> 00:23:08.960
first way

00:23:09.760 --> 00:23:15.060
is to not know the vows

00:23:15.620 --> 00:23:19.700
and that's a good way to break them.  If you want to break them,

00:23:19.700 --> 00:23:21.300
then don't study them and

00:23:21.640 --> 00:23:25.600
one of the things that bothers me... I have a lot of things that annoy me about the Dharma,

00:23:26.660 --> 00:23:32.360
is teachers who give initiations, huge initiations,

00:23:32.360 --> 00:23:37.200
and they don't explain to the people they're initiating

00:23:37.600 --> 00:23:40.120
that they've just taken vows.

00:23:40.160 --> 00:23:43.380
There are hundreds of vows you take when you receive an initiation,

00:23:44.320 --> 00:23:46.960
and you will [certainly] break them if you don't know them.

00:23:46.960 --> 00:23:49.780
It is the teacher's responsibility to

00:23:50.800 --> 00:23:54.000
prepare you regarding the vows before giving you an initiation.

00:23:54.960 --> 00:23:59.520
If they don't offer to train me, [I] wouldn't accept an initiation from them.

00:24:00.800 --> 00:24:05.760
The best way to break your vows, the first way, is to not know them.

00:24:06.160 --> 00:24:08.000
Read the recipe before you start cooking.

00:24:08.880 --> 00:24:11.280
That's what Veronica tells me every time I cook.  The

00:24:12.640 --> 00:24:14.640
next picture.

00:24:15.520 --> 00:24:21.980
There's a lady who says, "Hey, it's no big deal."

00:24:22.140 --> 00:24:32.200
That vow about cutting down green plants without saying a prayer,

00:24:32.940 --> 00:24:39.020
seriously, that's a bit of an exaggeration.  It's a bit too much, it's not that important.

00:24:39.020 --> 00:24:41.520
There are just a few insects

00:24:41.680 --> 00:24:46.140
that might use that leaf from time to time as a roof.  It's no

00:24:46.140 --> 00:24:48.720
big deal.

00:24:49.080 --> 00:24:52.360
The second great way to break your vows

00:24:52.560 --> 00:24:54.010
is to have this attitude.

00:24:54.010 --> 00:24:57.839
"Oh, this oath is not that important, I keep the big ones."

00:24:58.799 --> 00:25:00.799
Next.

00:25:04.880 --> 00:25:11.020
If we have a klesha, meaning if we have some kind of negativity

00:25:11.360 --> 00:25:15.440
running through our mind, that's a very good way to break your vows.

00:25:15.600 --> 00:25:19.180
Being irritated by someone else or

00:25:19.600 --> 00:25:24.920
being obsessed with purchasing something or money or

00:25:25.200 --> 00:25:28.080
being addicted to watching Netflix at night.

00:25:28.720 --> 00:25:34.680
...By the way, it's not wrong to watch Netflix [movies], I'm talking about

00:25:37.500 --> 00:25:41.840
hurting someone else because you want to get home and watch Netflix.  That's a problem.

00:25:43.360 --> 00:25:45.447
This is called gang warfare.

00:25:45.447 --> 00:25:46.959
What is the story about?

00:25:50.799 --> 00:25:54.719
Always go after the biggest guy on the opposing side.

00:25:55.520 --> 00:25:57.520
Find out who the leader of the other side is,

00:25:58.160 --> 00:26:02.660
and don't talk, don't negotiate, don't yell at each other,

00:26:02.740 --> 00:26:05.520
just go up to him and hit him in the head.

00:26:06.080 --> 00:26:09.340
And then all the others [his colleagues] will give up.

00:26:09.580 --> 00:26:13.660
Identify your biggest bad habit,

00:26:13.760 --> 00:26:17.520
and go for it first.  That's how you take your vows.

00:26:18.320 --> 00:26:20.320
Next.

00:26:23.880 --> 00:26:29.220
...By the way, at my age, I wo

00:26:29.220 --> 00:26:32.320
n't tell you how old I am,

00:26:32.320 --> 00:26:35.760
but this whole young love thing

00:26:35.760 --> 00:26:38.640
is so ridiculous from the perspective of my age.

00:26:40.960 --> 00:26:43.360
I can say it from experience, because I had it.

00:26:44.960 --> 00:26:46.880
This...

00:26:46.880 --> 00:26:49.359
"Oh, she's the most beautiful woman in the world."

00:26:50.000 --> 00:26:52.000
"He's the most handsome guy in the world."

00:26:53.040 --> 00:26:58.160
First of all, my older brother

00:26:58.160 --> 00:27:01.440
said the funniest thing.  He said, "Do you like that girl?"  I said, "Yes."  He

00:27:02.080 --> 00:27:04.080
said, "Do you want to spend your life with her?"  I said, "Yes."

00:27:04.640 --> 00:27:06.640
He said, "First look at her mother."

00:27:07.679 --> 00:27:14.798
"Look at what her mother looks like." I said [her] mother looks terrible.  She's overweight, looks tired, and looks terrible.

00:27:15.440 --> 00:27:20.360
And he said to me, "Well, what do you think he looked like when he was young?"

00:27:20.720 --> 00:27:22.880
Think about this.

00:27:24.080 --> 00:27:28.160
If you are attached to a person's appearance,

00:27:28.880 --> 00:27:33.920
or to something physical, or to something that is not very important about a person,

00:27:34.100 --> 00:27:39.620
that appearance will change and you will see them get sick, you

00:27:39.620 --> 00:27:42.680
will see them get old, you will see them have diarrhea and vomit.

00:27:42.880 --> 00:27:46.720
If you're not lucky, at some point you'll see his entrails or on the operating table.  Do

00:27:47.600 --> 00:27:50.800
n't fool yourself into thinking

00:27:51.760 --> 00:27:53.760
that it's worth hurting other people

00:27:54.320 --> 00:27:59.200
to get the most beautiful woman or man you can have.  It's not worth it.  It won't

00:28:00.480 --> 00:28:07.199
last.  It's great to have a relationship, but have it for the right reason.

00:28:07.840 --> 00:28:09.840
Next.

00:28:11.520 --> 00:28:13.759
If you have an anger problem

00:28:14.640 --> 00:28:16.640
or get angry easily,

00:28:16.960 --> 00:28:19.600
then imagine giving that person

00:28:20.320 --> 00:28:24.080
something they would like to have.  This is called @maitre

00:28:24.799 --> 00:28:26.080
@jampa

00:28:26.080 --> 00:28:26.794
Love.

00:28:26.800 --> 00:28:32.020
Imagine, try to remember how nice it is to give someone

00:28:32.560 --> 00:28:34.831
something they like, something they want.

00:28:34.840 --> 00:28:36.880
Try to have this attitude.

00:28:37.280 --> 00:28:40.720
If you don't feel friendly towards another person,

00:28:41.520 --> 00:28:44.419
then imagine what it would be like to meditate on

00:28:45.520 --> 00:28:49.039
what it would be like to give them something they really like.

00:28:49.679 --> 00:28:51.679
Next.

00:28:52.720 --> 00:28:58.559
I'll give you a moment for this... I bet you don't remember what this is...

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:02.000
Tim cheats by looking ahead.

00:29:06.720 --> 00:29:08.720
What was that?  It's

00:29:09.600 --> 00:29:12.480
about pride.

00:29:13.279 --> 00:29:16.398
Pride is also an obstacle to keeping vows.

00:29:17.279 --> 00:29:20.799
And... one of the most common kinds of pride

00:29:21.520 --> 00:29:26.540
in a monastic setting, where this book was generally taught,

00:29:28.960 --> 00:29:33.920
is how much you know about the scriptures and how much data you have gathered

00:29:34.560 --> 00:29:35.780
throughout your life.  I

00:29:36.000 --> 00:29:39.920
really like that.  These Dharma teachings are very little known

00:29:39.920 --> 00:29:41.760
and the more you collect them, the

00:29:42.100 --> 00:29:45.760
more special you feel.

00:29:46.559 --> 00:29:51.487
Pabongka Rinpoche said, "All the Dharma you have ever learned in your life, all the things you have memorized,

00:29:51.487 --> 00:29:53.300
all the things you have debated,

00:29:53.300 --> 00:29:55.360
all the Geshe degrees you could ever have,

00:29:57.100 --> 00:30:02.820
compared to what is left to study... you know nothing."

00:30:03.100 --> 00:30:06.160
You are like a worm at the bottom of the ocean,

00:30:06.880 --> 00:30:08.799
which sometimes comes to the surface and looks at the stars.

00:30:11.520 --> 00:30:14.239
Many of these stars have planets around them.

00:30:15.120 --> 00:30:19.039
There are people on those planets.  There are things to know about these people.

00:30:20.000 --> 00:30:23.100
Here are the things we know,

00:30:23.280 --> 00:30:25.280
that we are so proud to know,

00:30:26.240 --> 00:30:32.420
they are a tiny tiny [very] tiny fraction of what you could know.

00:30:33.820 --> 00:30:35.840
So, don't be proud!

00:30:35.840 --> 00:30:37.840
Next.

00:30:41.680 --> 00:30:45.880
One of the great motivations for breaking your vows

00:30:46.240 --> 00:30:52.880
or commitments, morality, that will stop you from reaching nirvana, that will stop you from reaching

00:30:53.760 --> 00:30:56.260
the second level of Larm Rim -- personal nirvana --

00:30:57.279 --> 00:31:01.518
is to understand emptiness, to study emptiness.

00:31:02.960 --> 00:31:04.960
If you realize that the bad things

00:31:05.440 --> 00:31:07.440
someone else does to you

00:31:08.080 --> 00:31:11.880
come directly from what you did last week,

00:31:12.480 --> 00:31:16.900
then you won't make big mistakes.  The more you study emptiness,

00:31:17.519 --> 00:31:21.059
the more you study cause and effect, interdependence,

00:31:21.680 --> 00:31:23.920
which means that that person comes from my seeds,

00:31:24.980 --> 00:31:32.320
then the easier it will be for you to keep your vows.  It will be much easier for you.  So study, study, study!  I

00:31:34.160 --> 00:31:39.960
had a very old Mongolian professor who had tuberculosis and

00:31:45.360 --> 00:31:47.279
he would say,

00:31:47.279 --> 00:31:54.879
"That's good. You're so proud, you have such a huge amount of pride from Princeton and

00:31:55.600 --> 00:31:57.279
then the fact that you're a geshe,

00:31:57.279 --> 00:31:59.279
it's a big help, a big help... You're

00:31:59.340 --> 00:32:02.480
going to push yourself so hard

00:32:03.039 --> 00:32:05.039
just to look smart.

00:32:05.120 --> 00:32:10.200
That's luck, but later try to give it up.

00:32:10.500 --> 00:32:13.740
Study how to be a good person. It's very funny.

00:32:14.760 --> 00:32:17.520
On his deathbed, he gave me the text that Adam is translating. I

00:32:18.320 --> 00:32:20.320
remember that. The

00:32:22.559 --> 00:32:24.480
next one

00:32:24.480 --> 00:32:28.959
Technically is that the fourth cause? No.

00:32:29.039 --> 00:32:34.079
One of the causes of breaking vows or commitments

00:32:36.159 --> 00:32:38.239
is that in the modern world it's very hard

00:32:38.799 --> 00:32:44.479
to think about vows when you're so busy. When things are moving so fast.

00:32:45.120 --> 00:32:47.439
There's a thousand things to look at on the internet

00:32:48.240 --> 00:32:51.680
and life is moving so fast.

00:32:52.040 --> 00:32:57.220
It's hard to keep your self-awareness. Am I

00:32:57.220 --> 00:33:01.760
breaking my vows, doing things that hurt others?

00:33:02.400 --> 00:33:07.260
I have to  slow down, go back to your vows.

00:33:07.600 --> 00:33:13.300
And maintain a sense of awareness

00:33:13.680 --> 00:33:18.420
that you have commitments not to hurt others.

00:33:18.740 --> 00:33:22.640
The busier you are, the more mindful you need to be.

00:33:24.260 --> 00:33:29.697
It's even easier to get annoyed with your partner when you're really busy.

00:33:29.697 --> 00:33:31.840
He's trying to tell you something and

00:33:32.480 --> 00:33:34.959
you have 10 things going on at work and...

00:33:36.399 --> 00:33:40.799
"I don't have time to listen right now.  "My

00:33:41.360 --> 00:33:44.479
boss gave me 10 things to do."

00:33:45.039 --> 00:33:47.039
Those are the times when you need to slow down

00:33:47.840 --> 00:33:49.840
and come back to your vows.

00:33:49.919 --> 00:33:53.518
Don't forget your commitment to be nice to other people, even when you're

00:33:54.240 --> 00:33:56.240
really stressed, really busy.

00:33:58.480 --> 00:34:03.039
It's better to break a few business commitments than to

00:34:04.320 --> 00:34:08.720
get angry and stressed and not be nice to people.

00:34:09.839 --> 00:34:12.719
It's better to not pay a bill or miss a business meeting or

00:34:13.679 --> 00:34:16.158
not give your best at work

00:34:17.280 --> 00:34:20.479
if it means keeping your mind clear.

00:34:23.599 --> 00:34:25.599
Next picture.

00:34:26.079 --> 00:34:29.379
This is a lady buying something she doesn't need at the store.

00:34:31.839 --> 00:34:33.839
See if you remember this story.

00:34:35.359 --> 00:34:40.639
She said, "Oh, this box is so beautiful." She went to the store. She bought it...

00:34:41.200 --> 00:34:43.200
...What's that home improvement store, the

00:34:43.600 --> 00:34:47.080
place where you buy things for the home? Crate and Barrel.

00:34:47.680 --> 00:34:52.560
She went to Crate and Barrel in America. She said, "Oh, my husband is going to love this box."  She

00:34:53.120 --> 00:34:56.100
has no idea what she's going to use it for,

00:34:56.560 --> 00:34:58.560
but she's going to buy it.

00:35:02.960 --> 00:35:08.020
And when she gets home, her husband will say, "You're crazy, this is a worthless box."

00:35:08.020 --> 00:35:14.100
"We have enough junk in the house."  "Take her back."  "Get your money back."

00:35:15.440 --> 00:35:19.280
Should she go to the gas station and try to return it?

00:35:22.800 --> 00:35:28.320
No, that's not where she got the box. It's obvious, but we have to say it.

00:35:30.079 --> 00:35:32.079
If you buy a stupid box

00:35:32.720 --> 00:35:35.760
because you like it and you think your husband will like it, which he won't...

00:35:37.520 --> 00:35:39.759
and he convinces you to take the box back,

00:35:40.720 --> 00:35:44.639
don't take it back somewhere else. Take it back to where you bought it.

00:35:45.280 --> 00:35:47.280
What does that mean? You should

00:35:54.079 --> 00:35:56.579
pay me.

00:35:58.240 --> 00:36:00.240
When you have to confess

00:36:00.240 --> 00:36:02.079
because you broke a vow,

00:36:02.079 --> 00:36:04.799
try to go to the person who made you the vow.

00:36:05.760 --> 00:36:10.620
Confess to the person who made you the vow.

00:36:10.860 --> 00:36:14.480
Is it okay to confess alone at home?

00:36:16.240 --> 00:36:20.479
No, for vows that you took from other people, generally.

00:36:22.560 --> 00:36:24.560
If you didn't take a vow

00:36:24.720 --> 00:36:27.199
from someone else, then maybe it's okay to confess at home,

00:36:27.920 --> 00:36:32.600
confess in front of a Buddha statue or something. In extreme cases, it's okay.

00:36:33.040 --> 00:36:34.620
But,  In general,

00:36:35.120 --> 00:36:37.760
if you can go back to the person who made your vows

00:36:38.640 --> 00:36:43.839
and confess openly, do it shamelessly. We act shamelessly all day long.

00:36:44.400 --> 00:36:47.760
So be shameless when it comes to your vows, and say to yourself, "What the hell!"

00:36:48.480 --> 00:36:51.280
Go straight to your teacher and say, "I broke this stupid vow."

00:36:51.839 --> 00:36:55.279
And your teacher will say, "Wow, you're a really bad person."  You're like... "

00:36:56.000 --> 00:37:00.560
Get over it and then you'll feel so clean, you'll feel so good.

00:37:02.120 --> 00:37:05.940
You can be shy about a lot of things in your life, but don't be shy about your vows.

00:37:05.940 --> 00:37:09.560
If you break a vow, go tell someone

00:37:09.680 --> 00:37:12.880
and [that's] how you get rid of the... Get rid of the problem.

00:37:13.120 --> 00:37:18.680
If you hide it from yourself and if you work harder to hide it than to confess it

00:37:18.720 --> 00:37:21.840
or to keep your vow, then it's just stupid

00:37:22.100 --> 00:37:25.200
and you're not going to feel good. You're not going to feel clean.

00:37:26.079 --> 00:37:30.319
Be open with your teachers. I have this problem. I have this bad habit.

00:37:32.160 --> 00:37:36.300
The karma is broken, the seed is broken.

00:37:36.960 --> 00:37:43.440
Your teacher will say, "I've heard that before, you told me before." But be persistent and keep telling them.

00:37:46.960 --> 00:37:48.960
Next picture:

00:37:50.400 --> 00:37:52.960
It's about... Wait! Remember?

00:37:59.600 --> 00:38:02.860
Again, it's about honoring the

00:38:03.340 --> 00:38:06.100
little details of the vows.

00:38:07.020 --> 00:38:12.260
It's actually  a vow for monks, they should brush their teeth,

00:38:12.260 --> 00:38:14.940
with a stick called @SO SHING.

00:38:14.940 --> 00:38:17.040
It was a stick that you have to use to clean your teeth. You

00:38:17.200 --> 00:38:19.919
cut it out of a tree and you use it.

00:38:20.640 --> 00:38:22.640
It's a toothbrush.

00:38:22.960 --> 00:38:27.980
It's said that these monks should have their own toothbrushes and brush their teeth. It

00:38:30.400 --> 00:38:32.560
might seem like a small thing.

00:38:33.440 --> 00:38:37.460
"Wait, I'm trying to keep my tantric vow to go to Amitabha's paradise

00:38:38.160 --> 00:38:41.760
